# Temporal Warrior

## Lore

A lesser practitioner of magic whose training joins physical combat and temporal magic, favouring the dimensional pocket and distortion spells. Like the wizard the warrior is typically an evil or self-serving rogue, trained by the demonic raider to take what he wants: about 80% learned directly from a temporal raider and served six to fourteen years. A favourite ploy is to store weapons and gear in dimensional pockets and envelopes, and to disorient a foe with time and sensory deprivation magic and time warps. Skills lean to combat, assassination and breaking and entering. Black, grey or blue body armor, often medium or heavy and resembling the raider''s own head and natural armor, under flamboyant capes and cloaks of red, yellow and gold. Most (90%) travel on foot, renting or stealing a horse or hover vehicle when necessary.

## Random Insanity Table

The warrior rolls on the table in the Temporal Wizard''s entry (printed 69): once for the ten-year bond, twice for the fourteen-year bond. 01-10 Pacifist. 11-15 Phobia: god-like beings, especially alien intelligences. 16-20 Obsessed with fighting and competition. 21-30 Obsession: power. 31-40 Obsession: hates temporal raiders. 41-45 Obsession: timeliness. 46-50 Phobia: terrified of temporal raiders. 51-55 Obsession: danger. 56-60 Obsession: time is meaningless (always 3D6 minutes late). 61-65 Paranoid: creatures of magic. 66-70 The eternal pessimist. 71-75 Cruel streak. 76-80 Paranoid: dimensional travelers. 81-85 Fear of success (-3 initiative, -3 strike, parry and dodge, -15% skills under pressure). 86-90 Obsession: magic. 91-95 Disgusted by anything slimy. 96-00 Phobia: physical transformation.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'temporal-warrior');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'temporal-warrior';

